   "source": [
    "# Automatic Radiology Report Generation from Chest X-Ray Images\n",
    "## CNN–LSTM Encoder–Decoder Architecture on Indiana University (Open-i) Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "**Course / Project Identity:** Deep Learning (Modules 2–4: CNN, RNN/LSTM, Transfer Learning)\n",
    "**Dataset:** [Chest X-rays (Indiana University) - Kaggle](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/raddar/chest-xrays-indiana-university)\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "### Pipeline Overview:\n",
    "1. **Environment Setup & Data Download**: Fetching dataset via Kaggle API / IU Open-i.\n",
    "2. **Data Cleaning & Patient-Wise Split**: Merging CSVs, cleaning text, splitting by Patient `uid` (80/10/10) to prevent data leakage across views.\n",
    "3. **CNN Visual Feature Caching**: Passing images through frozen **DenseNet121** (1024-d) and saving `.npy` vectors (~40x epoch speedup).\n",
    "4. **Text Tokenization & Vocabulary**: Building vocabulary (min_freq=3) with `<start>` / `<end>` tokens and padding to max length 80.\n",
    "5. **CNN-LSTM Decoder Model**: Building Keras Functional API model with Image Projection (256-d) + Word Embedding (256-d) into LSTM (256 units).\n",
    "6. **Training with Teacher Forcing**: Categorical Crossentropy, EarlyStopping, and validation loss checkpointing.\n",
    "7. **Decoding Strategies**: Comparing **Greedy Search** against **Beam Search ($k=3$)**.\n",
    "8. **Quantitative Evaluation**: Computing BLEU-1..4 and ROUGE-L against Ground Truth & Most-Common-Report Baseline.\n",
    "9. **Qualitative Analysis**: Visualizing 6 test X-ray cases with generated findings vs ground truth.\n",
    "10. **Gradio Web Interface**: Launching live interactive demo."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1: Environment Setup & Dependencies"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!pip install -q tensorflow pandas numpy matplotlib nltk rouge-score gradio kaggle tqdm\n",
    "\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import re\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
